  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5566",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the pathogenesis of Panel leukemia (Carcinoma cell lines) through a multi-tiered mechanism involving the targeting of A704 and 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn affects the disease process. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a modulator of these compounds, potentially influencing their activity against leukemia cells. The final scores from the three paths indicate a consistent and significant relationship, with the highest score in path_278742, suggesting a direct interaction between Mollicellin N and the target compound 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which is known to target Panel leukemia cell lines. This implies that Mollicellin N may exert its effects by modulating the activity of this compound, possibly through competitive binding or regulatory mechanisms. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the same target compound supports the hypothesis that Mollicellin N has a role in the treatment of Panel leukemia, though further investigation is needed to elucidate the exact mechanism of action and the extent of its therapeutic potential.",
